{"id":"5ea835b976feaaff","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-hahn-banach-segment.md","title":"Hahn–Banach Separation","display":"thm-hahn-banach-segment — Hahn–Banach Separation","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-hahn-banach-segment","aliases":["58-thm-hahn-banach-segment"],"display":"thm-hahn-banach-segment — Hahn–Banach Separation","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-analysis2-locally-convex-space.md]]","[[58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset]]","[[../batch12/58-df-zfc-top5-closed-set.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-zfc-top5-open-set.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-hahn-banach-segment"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-hahn-banach-segment</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-hahn-banach-segment — Hahn–Banach Separation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"7d71608bc30daeda\" href=\"?note=7d71608bc30daeda\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-zfc-analysis2-locally-convex-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-zfc-analysis2-locally-convex-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"67cf48a2f6e27861\" href=\"?note=67cf48a2f6e27861\" title=\"58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset\">58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"4dc8b2d2e69010a2\" href=\"?note=4dc8b2d2e69010a2\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-zfc-top5-closed-set.md\">../batch12/58-df-zfc-top5-closed-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"473439958a92cf5b\" href=\"?note=473439958a92cf5b\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-zfc-top5-open-set.md\">../batch04/58-df-zfc-top5-open-set.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"f67456d74b418241\" href=\"?note=f67456d74b418241\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md\">../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"44867449c3df728b\" href=\"?note=44867449c3df728b\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md\">../batch02/58-df-zfc-top2-continuous-map.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\tau,\\mathcal P,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,0_X,A,B,C,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F},f\\in V\">\\(X,\\tau,\\mathcal P,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,0_X,A,B,C,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F},f\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcAnalysis2LocallyConvexSpace}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcAnalysis2LocallyConvexSpace}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> is the imported seminorm-generated locally convex-space predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop5ClosedSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop5ClosedSet}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S\\)</span> are the imported subset predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S\\)</span> are the imported explicit linearity and continuity predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> are the standard topology and field operations; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> is the identity over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> and real part over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S\\)</span> are the local typed abbreviations defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}convex\\text{-}in\\text{-}hahn\\text{-}banach\\text{-}segment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(C;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;C\\subseteq X\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall x,y\\in C\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1]\\;\n+_X\\!\\left(\\left\\langle\\cdot_X(\\langle1-t,x\\rangle),\n\\cdot_X(\\langle t,y\\rangle)\\right\\rangle\\right)\\in C.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}convex\\text{-}in\\text{-}hahn\\text{-}banach\\text{-}segment}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(C;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;C\\subseteq X\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall x,y\\in C\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1]\\;\n+_X\\!\\left(\\left\\langle\\cdot_X(\\langle1-t,x\\rangle),\n\\cdot_X(\\langle t,y\\rangle)\\right\\rangle\\right)\\in C.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional\\text{-}for\\text{-}separation}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,X,\\mathbb F,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S(f,X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}continuous\\text{-}linear\\text{-}functional\\text{-}for\\text{-}separation}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,X,\\mathbb F,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop2ContinuousMap}_S(f,X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hahn\\text{-}banach\\text{-}segment}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcAnalysis2LocallyConvexSpace}_S(X,\\tau,\\mathcal P,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,0_X)\n\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\bigl(x\\neq0_X\\to\\exists p\\in\\mathcal P\\;(p(x)&gt;0)\\bigr)\n\\land\\varnothing\\neq A,B\\subseteq X\n\\land\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(A;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\n\\land\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(B;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\Bigl[\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(A,X,\\tau)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop5ClosedSet}_S(X,\\tau,B)\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{72pt}{}\\to\\exists f\\in V\\;\\exists\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\land\n\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(a)&lt;\\alpha&lt;\n\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(b))\\bigr)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{28pt}{}\\land\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(X,\\tau,A)\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\n\\to\\exists f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\land\n\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(a)&lt;\n\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(b))\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}hahn\\text{-}banach\\text{-}segment}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcAnalysis2LocallyConvexSpace}_S(X,\\tau,\\mathcal P,\\mathbb F,+_X,\\cdot_X,0_X)\n\\land\\forall x\\in X\\;\\bigl(x\\neq0_X\\to\\exists p\\in\\mathcal P\\;(p(x)&gt;0)\\bigr)\n\\land\\varnothing\\neq A,B\\subseteq X\n\\land\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(A;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\n\\land\\mathrm{ConvexIn}_S(B;X,+_X,\\cdot_X)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\Bigl[\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(A,X,\\tau)\n\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop5ClosedSet}_S(X,\\tau,B)\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{72pt}{}\\to\\exists f\\in V\\;\\exists\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\land\n\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(a)&lt;\\alpha&lt;\n\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(b))\\bigr)\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{28pt}{}\\land\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(X,\\tau,A)\\land A\\cap B=\\varnothing\n\\to\\exists f\\in V\\;\\bigl(\n\\mathrm{ContinuousLinearFunctional}_S(f;X,\\tau,\\mathbb F,\\tau_{\\mathbb F},+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\\land\n\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(a)&lt;\n\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}f(b))\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The first implication strongly separates a compact convex set from a\ndisjoint closed convex set; the second separates a disjoint open convex set\nfrom a convex set.  Nonemptiness, convexity, topology, and continuity are\nnow part of the antecedent.</li>\n<li>The Hausdorff condition is the displayed point-separation clause for the generating seminorms.  Continuous functionals are expanded using the actual eight-place linear-map and five-place continuous-map predicates.</li>\n<li>Minka–Stone theorem characterizes when linear functionals separate points.</li>\n<li>Consequences: Krein–Milman (extreme points), separation of closed convex sets.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-zfc-analysis2-locally-convex-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"7d71608bc30daeda","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-zfc-analysis2-locally-convex-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset","status":"resolved","id":"67cf48a2f6e27861","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-zfc-top5-closed-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"4dc8b2d2e69010a2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-zfc-top5-closed-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-zfc-top5-open-set.md","status":"resolved","id":"473439958a92cf5b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-zfc-top5-open-set.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元